Revision history for Perl-Critic-Policy-ValuesAndExpressions-ProhibitDescendingRanges

0.001 2026-11-04 TEODESIAN
    - Initial Release.  Reports a range that counts down in list context,
      such as 10 .. 1 or 'aa' .. 'b', because perl's .. counts only up and
      gives an empty list for it.  Also reports a range from an expression
      to a small number, such as $n .. 1, which is empty for every $n
      above that number.  The flip-flop operator, which is .. in scalar
      context, is not reported.
